  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14212968/assets/2242cf493c6307d8c6f2dac778efe6f89ca4ba6f04203940076360613c8dc9b0.png)\n\nA $13\\,\\text{ft}$ support pole leans against a vertical wall, forming an angle $\\theta $ with the ground. The base of the pole $B$ is being pulled toward the wall at a rate of $2\\,\\text{ft/s}.$ At what rate is $\\theta $ increasing at the moment when the top of the pole $T$ is $5\\,\\text{ft}$ above the ground? Do not round the answer.\n\nThe angle is increasing at a rate of\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{rad/s}.$",
